== Recent News

- \[August 2021\] We released [https://arise-initiative.github.io/robomimic-web/ robomimic], a framework for robot learning from demonstration. It offers a broad set of demonstration datasets collected on robot manipulation domains, and learning algorithms to learn from these datasets.

- \[August 2021\] New [https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.03298 preprint] on a [https://arise-initiative.github.io/robomimic-web/study/ large-scale study] conducted with [https://arise-initiative.github.io/robomimic-web/ robomimic] for learning from offline human demonstrations.

- \[June 2021\] Our [https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.00375 work] on enabling spatial generalization in visuomotor control from human demonstrations using a structured hand-eye action space was accepted to [https://www.iros2021.org/ IROS 2021].

- \[May 2021\] Our work on collaborative teleoperation with [https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.06738 Multi-Arm RoboTurk] was nominated as a best multi-robot systems paper finalist at [http://www.icra2021.org/ ICRA 2021]!

== About Me

I am a PhD candidate in the [http://svl.stanford.edu/ Stanford Vision and Learning Lab], jointly advised by [http://cvgl.stanford.edu/silvio/ Silvio Savarese] and [http://vision.stanford.edu/feifeili/ Fei-Fei Li]. My work focuses on developing systems and algorithms to allow robots to leverage human insight for manipulation tasks. 

